{"id":"leetcode-389","version":1,"status":"approved","title":"Find the Difference","summary":"Given two strings s and t, where t is formed by shuffling s and adding one extra character, identify and return the added character.","statement":"Given two strings s and t, where t is formed by shuffling s and adding one extra character, identify and return the added character.","constraints":["t is a shuffle of s plus exactly one lowercase letter.","Return that added character, including when it duplicates an existing one."],"topics":["bit-manipulation","strings"],"prerequisites":[],"signature":{"name":"added_character","parameters":[{"name":"s","annotation":"str","adapter":"raw","source_parameter":null},{"name":"t","annotation":"str","adapter":"raw","source_parameter":null}],"returns":"str","return_adapter":"raw","node_policy":"values","result_mode":"return","mutated_parameter":null,"immutable_parameters":[]},"starter_code":"def added_character(s: str, t: str) -> str:\n    # Write your solution here.\n    pass\n","reference_solution":"def added_character(s, t):\n value=0\n for char in s+t:value^=ord(char)\n return chr(value)\n","brute_force_solution":null,"known_wrong_solutions":["def added_character(s, t):\n for char in t:\n  if char not in s:return char\n return t[0]\n","def added_character(s, t):\n return t[-1]\n"],"target_time_complexity":"O(n)","target_space_complexity":"O(1)","estimated_minutes":20,"rubric":{"algorithmic_insight":1,"prerequisites":1,"implementation":1,"performance_pressure":0,"edge_cases":0},"hints":["Equal character occurrences cancel between the two strings.","XOR the code point of every character in both strings.","Convert the one remaining code point back to a character.","XOR is commutative and x XOR x is zero, so shuffle order is irrelevant."],"editorial":"XOR is commutative and x XOR x is zero, so shuffle order is irrelevant.","tests":[{"id":"lc-389-1","arguments":["abcd","abcde"],"expected":"e","comparator":"exact","visible":true,"explanati